{
  "id": "classical-probability",
  "term": "classical probability",
  "definition": "Classical probability is a rule-based way of judging likelihoods in which probability estimates are expected to stay consistent with standard constraints, such as conjunction and disjunction rules and the requirement that two complementary outcomes add up appropriately. In this context, it refers to a coherent, internally consistent form of probabilistic reasoning against which human and model judgments can be compared.",
